OL,3,GNEWSASEND children face losing tuition
OL,4,Ain September
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe families of dozens of children with
OL,7,Fspecial educational needs (SEND) in
OL,8,FSurrey say they are at risk of losing
OL,9,Ftheir tuition from next week.
OL,11,FWith days to go until the new academic
OL,12,Fyear begins, Surrey County Council has
OL,13,Fyet to formally confirm support
OL,14,Fpackages for a number of families whose
OL,15,Fchildren receive alternative teaching
OL,16,Fbecause they cannot be taught in
OL,17,Fschool.
OL,19,FKim from Ewhurst, whose 14-year-old son
OL,20,FHarry is educated out of school, said
OL,21,Fher family has had a "summer of
OL,22,Funcertainty."
OL,23,APub: 27-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,328,320,200,140,0,100
